# Install.bat is a batch file: cmd.exe reads it, and it is written for CRLF
# regardless of what a clone's core.autocrlf happens to be.
Install.bat text eol=crlf

# members.txt is read a line at a time by three different readers — the workflow's
# shell, the consumer project's CMake, and the installer check's cmd — and a
# carriage return would end up inside the last field of a line for two of them.
# Any clone with core.autocrlf set would hand it out as CRLF, so it is pinned the
# other way round: it is data, and all three readers take LF.
members.txt text eol=lf
